WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:02.890
Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson can kind of do it
all.

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:06.830
Successfully transitioning from a career as
one of the most popular and accomplished wrestling

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:11.099
stars of all time, he's gone on to a Hollywood
career that's spanned everything from action

00:00:11.099 --> 00:00:15.669
flicks like the Fast and Furious franchise
to family films like The Tooth Fairy to comedies

00:00:15.669 --> 00:00:17.210
like Central Intelligence.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:21.810
Johnson is a likable guy who always seems
happy to be wherever he is, and he never takes

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:25.020
himself too seriously, particularly on movie
sets.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:28.640
Here's a look at some bloopers that make us
love The Rock even more.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:30.259
Walking Tall

00:00:30.259 --> 00:00:35.120
Johnson is tough—the kind of guy who could
easily smash things without a need for special

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.710
props or stuntmen to do the dirty work for
him.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:40.180
At least one would think that would be the
case.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:44.440
When the wrestler was cast in one of his first
major lead roles, as Chris Vaughn, Jr. in

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:49.170
the 2004 remake of the '70s classic Walking
Tall, he discovered that his toughest enemy

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:54.640
wasn't the bad guy at all, but rather a particularly
obstinate car taillight.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:01.720
"I'm strong, I swear."

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:04.059
Journey 2: The Mysterious Island

00:01:04.059 --> 00:01:09.760
A not-so-little-known fact about Dwayne "The
Rock" Johnson: dude is seriously jacked.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:14.520
His muscles are absurdly large, so on the
set of Journey 2: The Mysterious Island, he

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:19.390
decided to let his body do the talking instead
of his mouth, to hilarious effect.

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:20.120
"What is this place?"

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:25.860
The Game Plan

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:29.860
It's almost like Johnson went full "Method"
actor with this blooper.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:34.250
In The Game Plan, he plays a star quarterback
who's thrust into the wackiness of fatherhood

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:36.690
upon suddenly learning he has an eight-year-old
daughter.

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:40.650
But it turns out there are certain pitfalls
involved in having a tea party when you're

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:42.720
as massive as The Rock.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:45.480
"Small chair, big guy.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:46.760
Classic."

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:50.120
The Other Guys

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:54.510
It looks like Johnson had cold feet when it
came time to film his big scene in the cop

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:59.080
comedy The Other Guys, in which he briefly
co-starred opposite Samuel L. Jackson.

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:02.450
The two extra-awesome detectives end up jumping
off a building.

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:04.530
At least, they're supposed to.

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:05.520
"Ahhhhh!

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:08.320
Whoops."

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:13.300
"I didn't know we were supposed to ---"

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:14.840
Central Intelligence

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:18.500
In this clip, Johnson shows he's not too tough
to take a little ribbing.

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:22.470
After he admits to the character played by
comedian Kevin Hart that his name is made

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:27.230
up, Hart gives him a pep talk, arguing that
having a made-up name isn't such a big deal.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:31.290
Hart then rattles off a bunch of cool names
that everybody knows aren't real, including

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.370
someone very familiar to Johnson.

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:35.080
"You think, uh…

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:37.950
Mr. T, and Sting, and the Rock?

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.350
You think those guys are real?

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:44.330
Those are a bunch of dumbass nicknames by
a bunch of dumbass people."

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:45.330
The Tooth Fairy

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:50.100
Well, there's a magazine for everything and
everyone: even tooth fairies.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:54.370
In this blooper from the set of the family-friendly
comedy The Tooth Fairy, in which Johnson plays

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:59.800
against type as…a tooth fairy, he shows
that he's still a man—a man with needs.

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:11.700
Race to Witch Mountain

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:16.640
Johnson keeps the mood light and shows he's
got some pretty agile improv comedy skills

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:19.840
for a guy best known for big and flashy action
movies.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:23.490
During the filming of this Disney remake,
Johnson yells out the names of a bunch of

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:28.209
different animals in an attempt to distract
another character, including one very dangerous

00:03:28.209 --> 00:03:30.030
animal in particular.

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:30.520
"Is that a woodchuck?

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:31.220
Ferret?

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:32.220
Kangaroo?

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:36.840
Vin Diesel… guy's better lookin."

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:40.060
Fast Five

00:03:40.069 --> 00:03:44.450
Speaking of Vin Diesel, here's Johnson messing
around on the set of Fast Five.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:48.870
He's only pretending to mercilessly pummel
Vin Diesel about the head and face, over and

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:53.680
over again, though according to internet rumor,
he probably wishes he had unloaded for real

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:54.900
when he had the chance.

00:03:59.069 --> 00:04:00.360
Thanks for watching!

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:02.819
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:02.819 --> 00:04:04.920
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

